            <ArticleTitle>Neuromodulation for chronic refractory angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>269-78</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neuromodulation is the use of therapies which alter the relationship between the heart, its autonomic innervation and the central nervous system with the objective of reducing the ischaemic burden and diminishing the perception of angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
